+# Independently prepared Direct inputs (A1, A2, B)
+
+This route prepares real library inputs in separate bounded stages. It avoids
+making the Direct compiler depend on Typed14's complete multi-language output
+preservation, and does not increase the maximum of64 selected roots. It makes
+no C++ source-compatibility, native execution, DDS, simulation or performance
+claim. The v1 Typed14, standalone, modular and profiler routes remain available.
+All examples below are argument shapes: Root must supply actual observed full7
+pins and fresh paths. There is no prospective inode, future manifest or copied
+success status in these examples.
+
+## A1: official C++ input
+
+Follow `CPP_LIBRARY_INPUTS.md`. `prepare_cpp_library.py` requalifies the genuine
+successful standalone object under its full original58-root closure, copies the
+object and finite official proof leaves to exclusive real new inodes, and lets
+normal `Frame.finish` publish the terminal report. The original `.d` retains its
+old absolute target and names; explicit copy associations are not a new compile.
+An inner qualifier sidecar is metadata only and is insufficient as an A1 result.
+A1 must finish successfully with source/input/root preservation and no owned
+copy descriptors left open. The original CPP report stays unchanged.
+
+## A2: terminal native GO24 input
+
+Run the *new frozen source's* `tests/ros_unitree/prepare_native_family_library.py`
+with `--source`, `--manifest`, `--manifest-sha256`, `--config`,
+`--config-sha256`, `--selection-input` and `--out`, exactly like A1. The selected
+JSON has format_version1, kind `uwvm-native-go24-library-selection-v1`, a
+`native_report` input label, an `upstream` name from Frame.upstreams, and finite
+explicit `restart_mappings`. The source-bound entry first proves the actual
+closed current64GiB/swap0/original CPU/leaf incarnation before importing helpers.
+No compiler, exporter, process or Guest starts in A2. Its metadata coordinator
+has a768MiB RSS ceiling and3600-second deadline; parent/current cgroup and all
+ancestor backing reserves remain enforced by Frame/Root ownership.
+
+A2's historical root is the **real terminal C52 report**:
+
+- Actual raw bytes40,555,414; SHA256
+  `c52bc5ed98e52904f52e1f8dac7031cd65a53f94d5128375d8de2eea23ae4d73`.
+- Its original full7 retains device68, inode326925 and actual original times.
+  The selected current report has its independently observed real full7. Any
+  device-only bridge is explicit; equal bytes do not excuse changed inode/times.
+- All forty original commands, three family statuses, normal/mount cleanup and
+  preservation facts must be genuinely successful. Native6's later raw failure
+  is never selected as a terminal native build or relabelled.
+- Whole original Source30 and its actual manifest, all23 original selected
+  roots, complete execution SDK, complete GO-derived tree and native prefix are
+  requalified. The execution SDK must additionally be an exact Frame root
+  with its saved complete admission catalog; the GO-derived/prefix subtrees
+  have genuinely zero symlinks. The additional complete metadata parents needed to read the SDK
+  acquisition report, old native control files and Source30 manifest must be
+  explicitly selected too. Root must construct the actual finite root union;
+  A2 never widens a root from an arbitrary embedded file name.
+- External regular targets already recorded by a complete original/current
+  source-root symlink catalog use the separately reviewed finite observational
+  ledger in `independent_cpp_object.catalog_pair(observed_targets=...)`. Each
+  actual source alias, original/current row, full target stream and explicit
+  source-root device bridge remains attached to that observation. A2 calls
+  `preserve_catalog_observations` after all proof/copy work. These targets never
+  enter Frame inputs/pins or Evidence.cache, cannot authorize parent/provider
+  roots, and cannot satisfy actually consumed compiler MD/official leaf access.
+  Those ordinary inputs retain exact selected-root admission. Default catalog
+  callers remain strict; a dynamic subtree inventory cannot grant this role.
+- The selected Unitree upstream has the real exact Git commit, complete whole
+  repository, actual all-blob acquisition proof and lock. Frame validates every
+  recorded official blob; profile strings alone are not acquisition evidence.
+- All195 package TUs and the one identity-export TU have their real configured
+  database, actual Make cwd/argv bijection, last-MF/all-MT semantics, complete
+  ordered system/header MD closure, fresh-before-build objects, GNU trace inputs,
+  original link scripts, eleven package DSOs and exporter ELF reopened.
+- Original stopped exporter proof binds actual opened map_files, same process
+  birth, physical executable/DSOs and one resume/`I` gate to actual metadata
+  stdout. It is historical process evidence. A2 only reopens physical files at
+  rest, never `/proc` paths from the retired process. Raw maps device numbers
+  stay separate from actual st_dev. DT_NEEDED aliases resolve to actual mapped
+  files, including real versioned SONAME symlinks; basename guesses are refused.
+- C52 captured no CMake FileAPI. A2 explicitly states NOT_CAPTURED and makes no
+  FileAPI qualification claim. Requiring FileAPI needs a genuine fresh build.
+
+The actual materialization, source selection, binder and generation receipts
+must associate every one of the24 complete definitions, bounds, native root and
+component IDs and adapter codec IDs. All eleven generated message-only files
+are carried forward unchanged. No schema, RIHS or field is invented to fill a
+missing metadata record. Original Source30 emitter digests and complete manifest
+remain separate from the later actual current emitter used by B.
+
+A2 exclusively copies the catalog,24 definitions, all eleven provider files,
+generation receipt and finite immutable proof documents into `out/library`.
+Each ordinary copied file is mode0400, nlink1, separately allocated, completely
+stream-hashed and fsynced through held nofollow source/destination descriptors.
+No hardlink, source chmod, SDK mutation or hidden fallback copy is permitted.
+Normal Frame.finish really reopens every distinct consumed full7 and complete
+input root before writing terminal kind
+`uwvm-independent-native-go24-library-input-v1`, status
+`PASS_INDEPENDENT_NATIVE_GO24_LIBRARY_INPUT_COPIED_AND_PRESERVED_NOT_EXECUTED`.
+Its old whole-root observations are facts at A2's stage only.
+
+**Generated-provider scope:** C52 compiled the official native package and
+identity exporter, then emitted native conversion/registry source. It did not
+compile those newly emitted headers into a Gateway. A2 says so explicitly.
+Native74's distinct completed at-rest qualification and the downstream current
+provider/full-MD Gateway check remain mandatory for owned physics/transport.
+A2 is not a substitute for that independent Runtime input chain.
+
+## B: actual standalone or modular Guest compilation
+
+First create a small real current Frame for the new source and actual used
+WASI/compiler/archive/QuickJS directories, completed A1 and A2 output roots, and
+fresh request controls. Do not copy A1's58-root list or A2's native root list into
+B. All actual consumed headers/tool archives still need complete selected root
+coverage. The new metadata-only entry
+`tests/ros_unitree/prepare_direct_library_configuration.py` consumes the closed
+v2 request template in `acceptance/independent_library_inputs`.
+
+Its ten tool labels and four SDK paths are explicit. It independently consumes
+completed same-source/current64 A1/A2, reruns the official copied source parser,
+reopens the unchanged original full-MD rule with explicit original→copied leaf
+associations, and checks actual compiler/sysroot/archive association. It writes
+an actual read-only selection/configuration and an **unexecuted literal argv**
+under its output controls. Root only uses this after normal terminal finish.
+There is no tool discovery, package fetch, guessed tool version or Typed14 input.
+
+The published selection kind is one of:
+
+- `unitree-direct-go2-standalone-independent-build-selection-v2`;
+- `unitree-direct-go2-modular-independent-build-selection-v2`.
+
+Root then invokes the actual `prepare_direct_guests.py` argv. This is a real B
+build, not metadata qualification. It always runs the actual current generator
+in a fresh directory, requires exactly the same24 native/codec identities and
+all eleven original generated output bodies, and retains its actual argv,
+complete definitions and source-bound emitter pins. Its generation admission
+kind is `uwvm-unitree-independent-go24-current-generation-admission-v2`.
+It honestly marks C52 generated-provider bytes as source-only and requires the
+separate native Gateway qualification before execution.
+
+C, C++ and embedded-JS denied/positive mains are all really compiled, linked,
+full-MD/trace checked and binary-validated. Standalone remains same-main with no
+preloads. Explicit modular mode builds three pure Wasm providers for actual
+LowState perception, motion and ordered Wasm callbacks, and the protocol root;
+it retains the existing native matched simulation kernel and profiler features.
+There is no physical robot, camera/image-vision claim, optional WASI grant,
+automatic ROS right or conversion of a multiprocess design into one process.
+
+## Owned physics and profiling
+
+After B actually completes, call
+`direct_independent_inputs.configuration(frame, api, base_config_input,
+base_physics_input, build_input)` from an admitted metadata-only Frame. It checks
+all actual B receipts, copied A1 object/MD closure and A2 lineage. The original
+C52 generation role, not its copy's path, must match the baseline native family.
+It adds B's actual minimal consumed whole roots and output root to the existing
+native/Worker/MuJoCo base configuration, requiring at most63 roots so CP310's
+exact runtime-control root still fits. It never adds preparation-only roots.
+
+Modular mode uses the existing modular adapter. Standalone keeps the original
+physics selection schema and empty preload route. Both return actual published
+configuration/template full7 pins, without forecasting a namespace or starting
+an actor. The ordinary CP310 `--phase run`/`--phase profile` owners remain in
+charge of actual private namespace, real Worker/Native opened mappings, actual
+VTune attach/lifetime, matched native replay, rights and cleanup. Those owners
+still independently require Native74-at-rest8503/current-provider full MD;
+no claim is inferred from A2's source-only provider copy.
+
+## Regression and execution status
+
+A1 has ten authored policy/kernel-copy regressions. The additional
+`test_native_family_inputs_policy.py::suite` returns eighteen DATA regressions
+using the real pinned original C52 report, actual GO documents/current profile
+and actual original export verbose log. It checks genuine terminal/cleanup,
+refusal to promote Native6 failure, raw hash/partial commands, all24 identities,
+component/codec/bounds mismatches, output inventory, and the actual Make argv
+bijection including missing/duplicate commands and altered cwd evidence. Root
+must supply the current64 guard and genuinely pinned data; suite construction
+runs no test. None of these tests, A1/A2, real generation, B compilation, DDS,
+physics or profiling was executed by this source author.
+
+All new source, patch and manifest hashes are review artifacts. Only actual
+Root runs after a complete fresh source freeze can establish terminal A1/A2/B
+results. Existing frozen sources and original raw success/failure reports stay
+unchanged. A failed preparation/output remains visible and cannot be reused as
+a success by copying a status string.
